// Generated by Windows/tools/export_logic_catalog.py.
export const LOGIC_HELP={"hardware.can.configure":["Configures the MCP2551/TWAI bus at 125, 250, 500 or 1000 kbit/s. Starts listen-only. Disable Listen only to transmit and acknowledge. Reconfiguration clears queues; correct wiring before recovering bus-off.","On Start -> Configure.In; set Listen only false, then Configure.Out -> Send.In. MCP2551 requires 5 V power and a 5 V to 3.3 V level shifter on CRX."],"hardware.can.send":["Queues one classic CAN frame. Decimal identifier, optional extended/remote flags, 0-8 space-separated hex bytes. Remote frames use Length and empty Data. Queued does not mean delivered. Transmissions make one attempt.","Timer -> Send.In; identifier 256, data 01 02 FF. Monitor Status.TX failed for missing acknowledgement."],"hardware.can.received":["Receives the latest frame with optional decimal identifier filter (-1 means any). Exposes flags, length and hex Data. Fast bursts can coalesce between Logics ticks; this is not a lossless recorder.","Received.Out -> MQTT Publish.In; Received.Data -> Publish.Text."],"hardware.can.status":["Reports controller readiness, bus-off and driver RX-missed/TX-failed counters. Counters reset on Configure. A missing peer or wrong bitrate can cause transmit failures.","Bus off -> Rising edge -> an alarm. Repair wiring/bitrate before using Configure to restart."],"hardware.modbus.read":["Queues a nonblocking MS1285 Modbus RTU read. Unit IDs 1-247, functions 1-4, zero-based address and count 1-32. Queued fires before the reply. Busy rejects overlapping requests. Serial settings are shared with the LCD/web monitor.","On Start -> Read.In. Received.Out -> an action; Last read value.Value -> its numeric input. Use a timer plus Status.Busy to poll without overlapping requests."],"hardware.modbus.received":["Fires for a new CRC-valid received frame. Unit filter 0 accepts all units; 1-247 limits it. Hex includes the complete captured frame up to the monitor limit. Rapid bursts can coalesce between Logics ticks. Invalid CRC frames appear in the monitor but do not trigger this event.","Received.Out -> MQTT Publish.In and Received.Hex -> MQTT Publish.Text. Set an exact MQTT topic."],"hardware.modbus.value":["Unsigned register/coil value at index 0-31 in the last successful read. Available is false while reading or after an error; an unavailable value is not zero.","Received.Out -> IF.In, Available -> IF.Condition, IF.True -> Plot.In and Value -> Plot.Value."],"hardware.modbus.status":["Reports whether a read is queued or waiting and the last result, exception or timeout. These signals use the same state as the web and LCD RS485 controls.","Status.Busy -> NOT -> Gate.Enabled; Timer.Out -> Gate.In -> Read.In."],"timing.countdown":["One-shot countdown, default 5 seconds. Start restarts the full duration. Reset restarts an active countdown or restores an idle timer. Stop cancels without Finished. Remaining (s) shows live time and can feed Plot/Save Data; Running is Boolean. Group Pause preserves time. Duration is captured at Start/Reset.","On Start.Out → Countdown Timer.Start; Finished → Built-in LED.Toggle or GPIO.Toggle. Connect another event to Reset or Stop. Range: 0.001–86400 seconds."],"clock.alarm":["Calendar alarm using UTC/NTP, a manually set clock, or one DS3231 RTC. Choose a specific date or checked weekdays, Monday first. All date/time fields use UTC. Alarm fires once per scheduled occurrence. Clock valid is false until the selected clock is trustworthy. Set clock applies the manual date/time to Manual or RTC only. Rearm clears occurrence history. Pausing/disabling does not replay missed alarms. Manual time is RAM-only; a battery-backed RTC retains time without power.","Alarm → LED.Toggle or GPIO.Toggle. For offline time add Sensor → DS3231 RTC, wire SDA/SCL and power, choose DS3231 RTC and set its clock once from live device Logics. For Manual choose Manual, enter a date/time, then use Set clock or wire an event to Set clock. Date range: 2000–2099."],"hardware.sleep":["Light sleep resumes RAM; Deep sleep restarts the device. Enable Wake timer (0.001-604800 seconds) and/or connect Wake GPIO. Awake fires only after light sleep. Rejected reports failure. CPU/web/software events cannot run during sleep. Audio/updates or busy storage reject sleep; recordings drain first. Motors stop before entry; external loads are not powered off.","Event -> Sleep.In; Wake GPIO.Source -> Sleep.Wake source; On Wake -> LED.Toggle. Release wake level before sleep. Deep sleep needs On Wake, not Awake. Avoid immediate boot-to-sleep loops."],"hardware.wake_gpio":["Hardware High/Low wake source. Deep sleep requires RTC-capable pins: ESP32 RTC pins, S3 GPIO0-21, C3 GPIO0-5, intersected with board availability and existing assignments. External pull resistor required. Software edges/conditions cannot wake a sleeping CPU.","Button/sensor interrupt -> selected GPIO; Source -> Sleep.Wake source. RTC alarm outputs may be wired here, but the software Alarm Clock does not run during sleep."],"event.wake":["Fires once after deep-sleep boot or successful light-sleep return, not cold boot. Wake cause uses the ESP-IDF enum: timer 4, GPIO 7, EXT0 2. Global/group modes still apply.","On Wake.Out -> LED.Toggle or measurement action."],"recording.interval":["Sets the cadence for Save Data and Transfer to Plotter. Accepts numeric or Boolean data. Duration units are milliseconds, seconds, minutes, hours or days; range 1 ms to 365 days. This controls sampling, while the Plotter requests buffered samples on demand.","Source.Value → Sampling Interval.Value; Sampling Interval.Value → Save Data.Value or Transfer to Plotter.Value. Without this node, both use 5 seconds."],"mainboard.save_data":["Records numeric and Boolean (0/1) samples every 5 seconds by default, while Logics runs. Insert Sampling Interval to change cadence. Uses external SD/SDMMC storage only and writes plain ASCII JSON Lines. Path is a directory (root by default); missing folders are created. Requires synchronized clock. Queued output confirms queue acceptance; storage errors appear in Plots.","Sensor.Value → Save Data.Value for automatic recording; optionally insert Sampling Interval. Use the same source with Transfer to Plotter.Value and matching plot/series names. Optional folder /measurements/room1."],"mainboard.plot":["Samples a numeric or Boolean (0/1) value every 5 seconds by default, or at a connected Sampling Interval. The Windows Plotter requests buffered samples over serial or Wi-Fi/IP; the device does not stream continuously. Give nodes the same plot name to overlay series in different colors.","GPIO.Analog raw → Transfer to Plotter.Value; Sampling Interval can go between them. Add a second Transfer to Plotter node with the same plot name and a different series name to overlay both."],"hardware.gpio":["Select an available GPIO and its mode: digital input, pull-up/down input, digital output, PWM, or analog read. Unsupported connectors are disabled. ADC1 remains usable with Wi-Fi. PWM uses up to two independent timers at 100-20000 Hz.","On Start.Out -> GPIO.Set level (High/Low) in Output mode; GPIO.Digital read -> Rising Edge.Value; Number.Value -> GPIO.Duty % and Timer.Out -> GPIO.Write PWM."],"hardware.led":["Controls the configured status LED or the board built-in LED. ON, OFF, Toggle and Set color take execution pulses. Brightness uses PWM for a regular LED and intensity scaling for NeoPixel/RGB LEDs. RGB color controls require NeoPixel/RGB hardware. Automatic status restores the network indicator.","On Start.Out -> Built-in LED.ON; Timer.Out -> Toggle; a shutdown event -> Automatic status."],"value.text":["Outputs the entered text, followed by an optional Number, Boolean or Text connected to Append value. Separator is inserted only when a value is appended.","Text \"Voltage: \" + Battery.Voltage → MQTT.Text or Display.Text."],"mainboard.mqtt.publish":["Publishes Text and an optional appended primitive value on execution. Topic must be exact (no + or #); QoS 1 and retained are configurable. Out means queued, not acknowledged.","Rising Edge.Out → Publish.In; Text \"Temperature: \" → Text; Temperature.Value → Append value; topic elma/alert."],"event.start":["Produces an execution pulse once when the logic runtime starts.","On Start → Play.In; File → Play.Source."],"event.change":["Produces an execution pulse whenever a Boolean changes, in either direction.","Compare.Result → On Change.Value → Play.In. This fires on both True and False transitions."],"event.rising":["Produces an execution pulse when a Boolean changes from False to True. The first available reading establishes a baseline; already True at startup does not fire.","Temperature → Compare > 50 → Rising Edge.Value; Rising Edge.Out → Play.In."],"event.falling":["Produces an execution pulse when a Boolean changes from True to False.","Device Enabled → Falling Edge.Value → Stop.In."],"condition.if":["Checks a Boolean and routes execution to True or False. A Boolean-driven IF can start a conditional chain in this editor.","Compare.Result → IF.Condition; IF.True → Relay ON.In. Use Rising Edge for a one-time threshold crossing."],"condition.between":["Returns True when Value is within the Minimum/Maximum range (inclusive).","Voltage → Between.Value, Minimum 11.8, Maximum 12.6 → IF.Condition."],"boolean.and":["Returns True only when both A and B are True.","Temperature > 30 and Device Enabled → AND → IF.Condition."],"boolean.or":["Returns True when at least one of A or B is True.","Low battery and Sensor error → OR → Rising Edge → Alert.In."],"boolean.not":["Inverts a Boolean: True becomes False and False becomes True.","Wi-Fi Connected → NOT → IF.Condition → reconnect action."],"flow.gate":["Passes an incoming execution pulse only while Enabled is True.","Timer.Out → Gate.In; Device Enabled → Gate.Enabled; Gate.Out → Play.In."],"flow.sequence":["Routes an execution pulse through First, then Second, in order.","On Start → Sequence.In; First → Relay ON; Second → Play."],"flow.branch":["On each execution pulse, checks Condition and chooses the True or False path.","Timer.Out → Branch.In; Compare.Result → Condition; True → Fan ON; False → Fan OFF."],"timing.delay":["Delays an incoming execution pulse by Seconds.","Rising Edge.Out → Delay.In, Seconds 5 → Relay OFF.In."],"timing.timer":["Produces periodic execution pulses using Seconds as the interval; accepts an execution start or Boolean enable.","Device Enabled → Timer.Enabled, Seconds 10 → sensor action."],"timing.repeat":["Emits Count total execution pulses: the first immediately, then every Seconds. New triggers during the active repeat are ignored.","On Start → Repeat.In, Count 3, Seconds 1 → Play.In."],"timing.debounce":["Waits for a quiet period of Seconds after incoming triggers, filtering rapid repeated input.","Button Rising Edge → Debounce.In, Seconds 0.05 → Toggle.In."],"timing.cooldown":["Allows a trigger, then suppresses additional triggers during the Seconds cooldown.","Alarm event → Cooldown.In, Seconds 30 → Play.In."],"audio.file":["Describes a device audio file. Use sd:/ or flash:/ paths; MP3, AAC, WAV, M4A and FLAC are supported.","Path sd:/media/alert.wav → Play.Source; Rising Edge.Out → Play.In."],"audio.tts":["Offline English alert speech, up to 256 characters. Speech rate 0.5–1.5, voice pitch 80–220 Hz, intonation 0–1. Lower rate improves clarity; higher intonation varies the voice. This small synthesizer remains robotic. Requires a DAC.","Text \"Temperature high\" → TTS.Text; Speech → Play.Source; Rising Edge → Play.In."],"audio.piano":["Holds one independent melody. Record replaces the previous melody; Play previews it. Mouse/PC keys record notes; select octave and instrument.","Melody → DAC Play.Source; Rising Edge → Play.In. DAC supports chords, passive buzzer one note, active buzzer timed beeps."],"audio.volume":["Adds per-source volume processing; Volume is 0–100%. It does not trigger playback.","File → Volume.Source, Volume 60 → Play.Source."],"audio.speed":["Changes per-source playback speed, 0.25–4×. It does not trigger playback.","File → Speed.Source, Speed 1.25 → Play.Source."],"audio.pitch":["Shifts per-source pitch by -24 to +24 semitones. It does not trigger playback.","File → Pitch.Source, Semitones 12 → Play.Source."],"audio.equalizer":["Applies three per-source EQ bands: 500 Hz, 3 kHz and 6 kHz, each -6 to +6 dB.","File → Equalizer.Source, Low +3 dB → Play.Source. Execution still connects to Play.In."],"action.on":["Turns the connected compatible peripheral on when execution arrives.","On Start → ON.In; Relay Peripheral reference → ON.Device."],"action.off":["Turns the connected compatible peripheral off when execution arrives.","Delay.Out → OFF.In; Relay Peripheral reference → OFF.Device."],"action.toggle":["Switches the connected compatible peripheral between on and off.","Button Rising Edge → Toggle.In; Relay reference → Toggle.Device."],"action.set":["Writes a numeric value to a peripheral that supports Set Value.","On Start → Set Value.In; Fan reference → Device; Number 50 → Value."]};
